.commandcode/taste/
node_modules/
outputs/
ref/
.runs/
.test-archive/
tasks/benchmark/results/
tasks/benchmark/*results*/
!tasks/benchmark/results/
!tasks/benchmark/results/*.md
!tasks/benchmark/controls/results/
!tasks/benchmark/controls/results/*.md
tasks/benchmark/results/.err-*.log4

# Routing-eval diagnostics, rewritten on every `npm test`. e1-misses.txt stays
# tracked on purpose: it is the regression record of which prompts failed to
# route, so a fix can be seen to hold. last-misses.txt is the baseline report
# from the same run, so tracking it only made every run dirty a tracked file for
# no information a reader could act on.
tests/routing/last-misses.txt

# Holds a credential supplied by whoever runs the benchmark. It was committed
# and pushed once with a hardcoded `||` fallback key, which is how a secret gets
# into a public repo: one `git add -A`. The script now reads the env var only
# and exits when it is unset, so there is nothing here worth tracking.
#
# AGENTS.md and docs/STEAL.md both already said this file must never be
# committed. The rule existed and nothing enforced it. That is a gate gap, not a
# documentation problem.
tasks/benchmark/run-api.mjs

# Local benchmark scratch, written by run-api.mjs and regenerated per run, like
# the other results-* trees above.
tasks/benchmark/results-api/

# Transcript-derived scratch: useful within a session, worthless in a clone.
.scratch/

# NOTE: a bare `tests/*` used to sit here. It matched the whole test tree, and
# because the existing suites were added before it they stayed tracked while
# every NEW test was silently ignored — so it ran locally and did not exist for
# anyone who cloned the repo. That is the "a name match is not execution"
# failure one layer down: a suite wired into `npm test` and absent from the
# repository. The tests are the source of truth for what this repo claims; they
# are not build output. scripts/tests-check.mjs now fails if this ever ignores a
# test again.

# `docs/` and `references/` are deliberately NOT ignored, and the reasoning is
# recorded here because this looks like an obvious candidate and it is not:
#
#   docs/STEAL.md             read by scripts/steal-selfcheck.mjs        (npm test)
#   docs/rejected-changes.md  read by scripts/rejected-change-ledger.mjs (npm test)
#   references/*.md           read by scripts/reference-reachability.mjs (npm test)
#   references/host-rules.md  the SOURCE for 112 generated host adapters
#   references/               listed in package.json#files — it ships
#
# Ignoring either makes a fresh clone unable to run its own test suite, and
# dropping references/ breaks the published package. Verified by hiding docs/:
# steal-selfcheck.mjs dies with an ENOENT rather than a clean message.
